Z||000000||fiero56||10-12-2001||09:05 PM||||I'm going to do it. I've been putting it off for over 2 months. I am going to take my Formula to e-check in the morning. Wonder what they will break this time. They are running a 100% record of breaking something every time I have a car there.<P>Few weeks ago they were testing an RX300, they jumped the rollers and totalled it. It happens much more often than one would think, much more often.<P>Since there is no employee parking lot(and no parked cars there other than "customer cars"), and it is inner city on a bus-route, I don't think the employees even drive, wonder if they even have a DL. You should have the seen them try to drive my 4-speed last time I had my SE there. Complete ignorance, there is no other word for it. I wish I had a video camera I could hide in the cabin. It would make for an excellent television show about bad drivers, who only drive 5 feet at a time.<P>Done ranting.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||13
Z||000001||Fformula88||10-12-2001||09:09 PM||||What is it for?  Is this some kind of state inspection or emissions inspection?  I apologize, but here in NY we don't have to have tailpipe emissions or have someone put the car on rollers.  Just curious.  It also sounds like its time to find one of those places out in a richer neighborhood where the workers are at least liscensed!||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||10-12-2001||09:15 PM||||In effect they are analy probing my baby, from both exhaust sides.<P>They throw the car on a dyno, drive it up to speed, measure the emmsions, and your done. IF you're lucky.<P>They force us suburbanites to drive into the city for this.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||10-12-2001||10:50 PM||||i turned in my blazer tags because of it. it passed the emissions part (after i got another person who could drive a stick to drive it. the first guy didn't shift beyond 2nd), but they found a broken air injection line and failed it. the parts are so corroded i just made it worse. it was such a beater i didn't want to keep trying to repair it so i let it go. got no love for 'em.<P>whats even better? once a year i give them the keys to my corvette.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||10-12-2001||10:57 PM||||well, you've got me started now.<P>it's also a great hinderance to an engine swap. anything '84 and newer not only has to pass emissions, they lift the hood and check for all the emissions equipment. my '74 chevy can actually pass using the numbers for my '87 coupe when it's tuned well, but that engine in a fiero will fail.<P>i just went to a car show last week and there were no new cars with much work done to them. if there was work done when you looked at the tag it was from another county or southern indiana. they're stifling the creative process.<P>ok, i'm done this time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||danny boy||10-13-2001||01:30 AM||||Emissions testing? Whats that? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">   <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||BlackStang95||10-13-2001||01:49 AM||||Thankfully I live in a state with no emissions test (they make us have license plates in the front and back though...) but I've seen a product in auto stores called G2P (Guaranteed To Pass) and it says it guarantees after use your car will pass your states test or double your money back.  It was like 15 bucks I think.  It might be crap, as I've never tried it, but I thought id share.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Flamberge||10-13-2001||02:10 AM||||You mentioned that the guys have jumped the rollers and totalled vehicles before... why don't they chain the car down? During my USAF days, we used to take F-15s over to the "hush house" (hanger where full AB engine runs can be done) and - you guessed it - run the engines in full afterburner. We used wheel chocks and a large chain to hold the arresting hook. Why can't they hook chains up to the frame and use chocks? That would make sense. I hate IM-ing cars, because everytime I have had it done, the person doing the tests always looks at me like I am trying to get away with something. &gt; <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Great rant topic!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>- Flamberge||||reg||5
Z||000008||thomas_l||10-13-2001||07:37 AM||||The reason an RX300 jumped the rollers is automatic 4 wheel drive - a co-worker has one.<P>When I got my 87 GT smogged (we have the dyno test in GA too) I was getting a laugh from the guy first finding the cat then figuring out it was RWD then trying to pick up a tach signal with the inductive wand over the <I>front</I> of the car. (this after already seeing the engine in the back while hunting for the cat with a mirror)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000009||Tina||10-13-2001||09:36 AM||||Perhaps you get lucky, last time mine went to the E-check, he couldn't drive it on to the rollers.<BR>(Minnesota wintertime, and he was wearing Sorrels...too big,or at least so he said.)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>I believe that was 2 years ago, since then they discontinued the testing of emissions completly.<BR>BTW In MN the car only would make it on to the rollers if it failed the the first E-check at idle.<P>Tina<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Master_Sushi||10-13-2001||10:08 AM||||Just give the guy 20 bucks or something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. Thats what allot of people do where I live. You should see some of the junkers here. In NY there are no emissions. They basicly seem to just look the car over and take off one wheel.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||10-13-2001||10:09 AM||||Thank God I live in a state with no inspections, emissions or otherwise.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||10-13-2001||10:23 AM||||Its all in where you take it in NY.  They are supposed to check over all the emissions equipment but no anal probes (I think NYC might have the anal probe, but not upstate).  The place I go sees so many junkers come in they think my Fiero is NEW!!  Its like an automatic sticker.  Check the brakes thru the wheels... who needs to pull one.  Make sure the lights work and the sticker goea on the window.  Forget any kind of detailed suspension checks!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>I hope they don't start tailpipe emissions anytime soon!  My Fiero would be in trouble!!||||reg||1
Z||000013||firstfiero||10-13-2001||10:43 AM||||      I read in the paper yesterday that here in my little town of York pa their not going to check any car made befor 1996. WOOHOO! I've been worried about this crap for a while. <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000014||fiero56||10-13-2001||12:59 PM||||Its a record! I got there at 7:45 am(they open the doors at 8am), and I was only one of 4 cars waiting for them to throw open the doors. I got onto the dyno at 8:09am. As I get out to let the tech in, I say, "can you drive a stick?", he just gives me this look like "who do you think I am". I told him, "don't fu## anything up this time, the car is RWD", and tossed him the keys. He only stalled twice getting to the rollers, and 4 times trying to get the dyno going(this is seriously a record in fewest stalls). After I get my car back I notice the steering column is wobbly from him banging the tilt several times. Thats ok, if it only took 3 hits to cause it, it must not have been too far away from happening. <P>Was talking to a lady while I waited, and she said her daughters car jumped the rollers last year, and they stopped it just as it hit the brick wall. <P>Now I need to see why I got an extension since I passed with no problem. This thing is supposed to be good for 2 years, not 3 months.<P>They use 1 wheel blocker type deal, hop in, and punch the gas. Once the monitors say the test is over, they drive off the dyno, and do the all important "gas cap test".<P>I got the pretty new Ohio plates for it too.||||reg||1
